WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
 What's up, Marvel fans?

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.060
We're here with Tom Holland,
who plays Peter Parker.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.850
This is one of the biggest
Spider-Man films ever made.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.930
What was your reaction
when you read the premise?

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:08.730
 Oh, man.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.670
I was blown away.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.800
I was also so skeptical.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.150
I just-- at the
time, I was like,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.650
there's no way that they
could pull this off.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.630
There's no way that
they'll be able to bring

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.490
these villains back
into this universe

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.080
and make it make sense.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:19.890
But they did.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.630
And they've done it in
a wonderful fashion.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.360
The movie is incredibly
heartfelt. It's funny.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.410
It's emotional.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:26.610
It's exciting.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.830
And you know, Jon
Watts has really

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.760
knocked it out of the park.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.430
So to be here tonight
celebrating this movie,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.430
I honestly cannot even begin
to explain to you how happy

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.630
I am and how excited I am.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.210
If you had told me 10 years
ago that you'll be playing

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.220
Spider-Man in a movie like
this, I would have been like,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.170
you're a liar.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.630
 Well, in a movie
like this, exactly.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.930
Look at all-- look
at all these people.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:46.800
They love you!

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.530
Movie like this-- you're playing
opposite super villains from

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.730
previous Spider-Man movies.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.020
What is that like?

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:52.920
 It's incredible.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.460
I mean, I've been a huge fan of
these movies since I was a kid.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.910
I remember seeing Toby's movies.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.340
I remember seeing
Andrew's movies.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.190
So to get the chance to share
the screen with their villains

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.300
has been one of the most
rewarding aspects of my career.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.500
And I'm so lucky
to be here tonight.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.170
I can't wait to share
the night with them.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.630
And I'm seeing Tom Rothman
over there, my boss who I

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.980
love who's been so kind to me.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.630
I want to go and
give him a big hug.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.750
And honestly, I
am beyond excited.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.270
 Peter goes through so much--
the death of Tony Stark,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.550
Mysterio letting him
know his entire identity.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.870
What is that like for
Peter Parker in this film?

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:26.670
 It's tough.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.800
I mean, everyone's been
asking me in the press,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.620
can you relate to it
because you're famous?

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.120
But I'm famous
for making movies,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.280
and he's famous for
being a mass murderer.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.960
So it's slightly different.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.510
But it's been a very
exciting challenge, something

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.220
I've really enjoyed
taking on, bringing

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.600
to life in the character.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.910
It definitely tonally
shifts the movie.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.680
It makes the movie feel very
different to the previous two,

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.480
which is great.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.470
I love change, and
I love this movie.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.690
And I love everyone here.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.100
And it's awesome.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.040
 Tom, you got a busy night.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.360
Enjoy the premiere.
Thank you so much.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.160
Thank you.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.030
Have a good one.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

